{"name":"Rosewater","hex":"#f6dbd8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rosewater","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A liquid produced by steeping rose petals in water, used as a coloring agent and a flavoring ingredient in certain foods."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rosewater"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosewater (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Rosewater is a 2014 American political drama film written, directed and produced by Jon Stewart, based on the memoir Then They Came for Me by Maziar Bahari and Aimee Molloy. It recounts Bahari's 2009 imprisonment by Iran, connected to an interview he participated in on The Daily Show that same year; Iranian authorities presented the interview as evidence that he was in communication with an American spy. Due to the content of the film, Stewart has been accused by Iran's state TV of being funded by Zionists and working with the CIA. The film was released in theaters on November 14, 2014. The film received generally positive reviews but was a box-office bomb, earning only a little over 3 million dollars."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9e/Rosewater_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosewater_(film)","wikidata":"Q14948398"},{"title":"Rosewater (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Rosewater is a point-and-click adventure game developed by Grundislav Games. The game tells the story of Harley Leger, a freelance writer who travels to the frontier town of Rosewater in an alternate history version of the American West. It is set in the same world as the studio's previous game, Lamplight City."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d2/RosewaterCoverPoster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosewater_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q122901805"},{"title":"Rose water","blocks":[{"text":"Rose water or rosewater is a flavoured water created by steeping rose petals in water. It is typically made as a by-product during the distillation of rose petals to make rose oil for perfumes. Rose water is widely used to flavour culinary dishes and enhance cosmetic products, and it is significant in religious rituals throughout Eurasia. Iran is a major producer, supplying around 90% of the world's rose water demand."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Golab_being_make_in_Meymand_-_Fars_21.jpg/330px-Golab_being_make_in_Meymand_-_Fars_21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_water","wikidata":"Q900450"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Rosewater_bottle%2C_Iran%2C_12th_century%2C_silver_with_gold_and_niello_-_Freer_Gallery_of_Art_-_DSC05289.JPG/500px-Rosewater_bottle%2C_Iran%2C_12th_century%2C_silver_with_gold_and_niello_-_Freer_Gallery_of_Art_-_DSC05289.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Rosewater_bottle%2C_Iran%2C_12th_century%2C_silver_with_gold_and_niello_-_Freer_Gallery_of_Art_-_DSC05289.JPG/1280px-Rosewater_bottle%2C_Iran%2C_12th_century%2C_silver_with_gold_and_niello_-_Freer_Gallery_of_Art_-_DSC05289.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Rosewater_bottle%2C_Iran%2C_12th_century%2C_silver_with_gold_and_niello_-_Freer_Gallery_of_Art_-_DSC05289.JPG/500px-Rosewater_bottle%2C_Iran%2C_12th_century%2C_silver_with_gold_and_niello_-_Freer_Gallery_of_Art_-_DSC05289.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"12th-century rosewater bottle from Iran (silver with gold and niello, Freer Gallery of Art, Washington, D.C.)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARosewater_bottle%2C_I